<section class="story section">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <div class="story__head">
      <h2 class="section-title">I Was the Agency Guy. Then I Got Tired of It.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="story__body">
      <p>For years, I ran a marketing agency. And I was good. SEO, Google Ads, content, citations, local pack domination — I knew how to move the needle for home service businesses. My clients were adding revenue. Their businesses were growing. Life was good. Except it wasn't. Because I kept doing the math, and the math kept bothering me. I was doing the work. I understood the market. I knew exactly why revenue went up. But I was taking home a management fee while my clients kept everything I built. Every dollar of growth I created went mostly to them. I was the engine, and they owned the car. So I stopped. I took every skill I had — every SEO framework, every Google Ads structure, every positioning strategy — and I applied it to my own company.</p>
      <p>I built The Mounting Man in the Twin Cities. TV mounting. Show-up is a black 2023 Tesla Model Y Performance, all black, two toolboxes, a vacuum. The Tesla drives. Best day: 2025-09-23, $6,458.10. Best week: 2024-12-01–07, $17,291.59. Best month: 2024-12, $59,798.23. Best year: 2024, $512,022.13. $2,152 is a package, not an average. 1,202 payments in 2024 is the overextension story: I made the money, contractors ate the profit, I pruned, I keep more. Not a volume target. Houston and Austin are tests. Not nationwide.</p>
      <p>Frame / mantel / porcelain / in-wall cable. Local SEO that actually ranks.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

